module gunbc.plans.v2_complexity_capability_parity

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn v2_complexity_capability_parity_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** restore v2 cost/complexity capability without porting the v1 AST or string identities. Design first; no implementation authorized by this note. This plan owns expressible/derivable cost, work/span, output size, space, summaries and recursion. Subject binding, input valuation, honesty/cost justification and witness admission belonged to the deleted discrete-cost-derivation sibling; they remain dependency obligations, not silently completed work."),
    p(text: "**Standing owners:** v2.lens.enforcement.contract distinguishes the blocking lens_contract_cost with BoundConsumerWitness/WallNow from AuditOnly complexity contracts without consumers. Derived kernel and accumulator-copy are WallAfterGrounding; linearity-audit targets SubstrateMandatoryTag; lowering targets SingleAuthority; optimality is OutsideModeledGuarantee. Re-read those carriers for current standing. The old mixed RatchetForever row is gone; never restore or simply relabel it. The constant-true complexity_variables_admits finding is carried by VacuousValidation plus execution, not inferred merely from its name."),
    p(text: "**Authority ruling (signed 2026-08-05):** v2.lens.cost owns grounded cost/size expressions, work/span, output/space and effect demand; v2.lens.complexity only projects asymptotic classes/dominance; std.realization_schedule owns resource accounts/scheduling; v1.compiler.complexity is inventory/parity oracle and deletion target. SymbolicCost is the normalized CostExpr projection, not a rival authority. Any future namespace move is atomic with every consumer repointed. The current blocking cost kernel and its consumer witness must stay green throughout."),
    p(text: "**Grounding:** use DeclarationRef through decl_ref_resolution for functions/collections; size identities use existing SizeVariable or a newly modeled authority before consumption. ValueIdentity was only a proposal, not an existing symbol. Replace CostExtern names with CostEffect.operation:DeclarationRef joined to ExecuteEffect; replace free-text unknown reasons with typed located countable causes; reconcile certainty with DescentEvidence and measured bases. Do not copy string-keyed SizeVar/SizeLen/extern/unknown/summary maps. Moving llvm_instruction_cost to a cited target model also changes lens_owned_fn_llvm_instruction_cost in the lens registry."),
    p(text: "**C0 receipts/limits:** v1_complexity_capability_census separates CostProgramRole, CostMigrationDestination (excluding the deletion target) and CapabilityFactProducer. v1_complexity_inventory_roster is inventory, not capability count: residue rows identify their capability. DeclRef checks refuse missing module, missing declaration and a name present only inside a note; List distinctness is an executed duplicate check, not construction. Every disposition arm has a control. v1_complexity_decl_classification derives the fn/type/data/let population from DeclFact, classifies every declaration exactly once as authority/helper/hazard/out-of-scope, rejects stale rows and requires each SemanticCapabilityItem to have AuthorityOf. This proves declaration coverage against the authored vocabulary, not discovery of an omitted semantic capability."),
    p(text: "**C0 execution boundary:** exact resolution/eviction controls live in test.claim.long.v1_complexity_capability_census_resolution and totality in test.claim.long.v1_complexity_decl_classification_totality, outside per-PR execution; ci_layer_roots names the recipe. Fast structural/classification witnesses do run per PR. The eviction control cached work 42 then observed an evicted Present zero-work/zero-span Proven summary while never-cached returned Absent: preserve this falsifier. cost_account_space_from_summary returned ByteSize? without CostAccount/Derived despite its note; prose is not a bridge receipt. [Original audit](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/v2_complexity_capability_parity.dag) retains dated inventory readings."),
    p(text: "**Boundary split:** bounded work/span/summation/output/space/evaluation, acyclic summaries and descent-grounded SCCs are decidable-but-unbuilt, AuditOnly until a real consumer and Blocking only after execution coverage. Unrestricted optimality remains OutsideModeledGuarantee until unrestricted_semantic_complexity_equivalence_procedure has a DeclFact row; authoring it must invalidate the boundary stamp. Catalog lowering is a different subject in complexity_lowering. No permanent RatchetForever classification or claim of arbitrary refinement completeness."),
    p(text: "**C1–C3:** C1 promotes grounded SizeExpr/CostExpr including branch max, binder-carrying bounded sums and effects; all existing cost witnesses remain green and exact bounded summation becomes representable. C2 restores work, span, output_sizes, peak_space, certainty and effect_demand. Sequential composition adds work/span and maxes space; parallel adds work/space and maxes span, matching realization_measurement. Equal-work graphs with different shape must derive different span; span cannot be deferred. C3 bounded-input valuation belongs to the sibling dependency and must land before C4."),
    p(text: "**C4:** declaration-keyed call graph/SCCs, memoized summaries, descent bounds and worklist/tree/cardinality shapes. Integrate existing std.graph, std.termination, std.computation, std.induction and v2.std.cardinality; their vocabulary is shared but v2 still owes integration and fact producers. Parser progress is a specialized consumer of v2 parser descent facts (advance token position, strict cycles, input-derived depth), not a core special case. ParserProgressFactProduction is migration-owed; ParserProgressV1Walker retires only after that capability executes. This is the largest unresolved slice; no v1 walker transplant."),
    p(text: "**C5–C7:** bridge summaries to CostAccount with Derived | PredictedFromCalibration | Measured PER RESOURCE AXIS, since time/space/power can have different evidence; pass the valuation/calibration omission RED. Add witness-cost admission, floor scheduling demand and an affected-graph O(n)→O(n²) regression wall, plus self-costing or a narrow justified exemption. Only then flip AuditOnly→Blocking; a split contract with NoConsumerWitness must refuse that flip. Finally reproduce or explicitly disposition every meaningful v1 conclusion before deleting/disposing the legacy realization. This program parallels self-hosting and does not block it, but further directory-driven long/ policy expansion deepens the proxy it is intended to retire."),
    p(text: "**Validation/parity:** flat/nested iteration, branch max, output growth, recursive trees, worklist drain, mutual parser recursion, external effects, unbounded refusal and parallel work/span. A bounded sum yields an exact count; shared summary reuse across two sites does not double-count derivation; removing descent from mutual recursion refuses rather than falling back to a class; complexity_variables_admits rejects at least one input. Review each specialized lens individually: subsumed→delete/repoint, useful→consumer/row, ungrounded→retain its frontier. C0’s signed ownership puts CostExpr migration here; seed shrink consumes that authority rather than deciding it."),
  ]
}

data v2_complexity_capability_parity_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "v2-complexity-capability-parity",
  title: "v2 complexity capability parity — restoring the engine, not porting the seed",
  body: v2_complexity_capability_parity_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the capability census is closed with every v1 row dispositioned, the boundary class distinguishes derived-kernel from optimality (SATISFIED: `lens_contract_complexity_derived_kernel` and `lens_contract_complexity_optimality` replaced the mixed row), v2.lens.cost carries grounded SizeExpr/CostExpr with work/span/output-size/peak-space/certainty on a restored ComplexitySummary, interprocedural summaries and descent bounds derive over declaration-keyed identities, the parity corpus reproduces or dispositions every meaningful v1 conclusion, `lens_contract_complexity_derived_kernel` has a live consumer witness and has flipped off AuditOnly — and this clause deliberately does NOT name `lens_contract_complexity_optimality` flipping Blocking: that row is `OutsideModeledGuarantee` until `unrestricted_semantic_complexity_equivalence_procedure` has a `DeclFact` row, and stays AuditOnly until a live consumer exists, so requiring IT to flip Blocking would make this doc unretirable by construction, and v1.compiler.complexity is deleted or dispositioned — at which point the carriers state the capability and this note retires.")
  }
}
